# CEFR lists: B1+ only

Site visitors are **intermediate to advanced**. A1/A2 on vocabulary or verb lists is a waste of time.

## Do

- Put only **B1, B2, C1, C2** (or untagged) ids on `word_ids` in `data/vocabulary-lists.json`
- Use `tools/cefr_policy.py` (`keep_word`, `is_beginner_cefr`, `filter_list_ids`)
- After building/importing lists, run `python tools/filter_lists_cefr_b1.py`
- Label list `cefr` as `B1–C1` (or a B1+ range), never `A1` / `A2`

## Do not

- Collect A1 or A2 onto any vocab list or verb-forms list
- Recreate packs like `target-a1-core`, `target-a2-bridge`, `path-week-1-survival`
- Wipe the whole lists file when adding a new pack — merge by list `id`

The **word bank** (`vocabulary.json`, `verb-forms.json`) may still store A1/A2. That is fine. Study lists must not include them.
